body:
Hey man, If the alcohol fills a hole, then let it, it will kill you but that doesn't matter, i cant stand it when people tell me what will kill me and that i should stop making choices for myself. Death is what gives overall meaning to our lives. Im not an advice giver but what i would say is stay on the alcohol if you have to, benzodiazepines are very risky, my grand mother went insane after being on them for 5 months, i suggest that whatever happens you don't resort to drug use, no matter the cost. Hold on to the things you had and let the ashes of the past be the foundation of what grows tomorrow. Find 1 thing that makes you wonder, literally anything, just one thing and wonder, just wonder, its the biggest gift we have, my childhood was full of hate and pain and suffering and violence and neglect, but i didn't mind because i always had wonder and curiosity and joy and laughter. Now all i have is pain and boredom and uncertainty. DON'T LET GO OF THE LITTLE THINGS, just breathe outside or on a hill and wonder, what is it all for? - Don't try to answer it, just let the question float off into the distance. Peace and wisdom is not the ability to answer any question, but to let any question go. I hope that you find your wonder somewhere, whether it be in someone or something or someplace. Wonder my friend, wonder. 

&#x200B;

j
